# Ejemplos ejecutables
#
# Compatible con la extensión "REST Client" de VS Code y con Thunder Client.
# 1. Levantar el servicio: make run
# 2. Crear una API key en http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin
# 3. Reemplazar el valor de @apiKey

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@apiKey = cck_reemplazar_por_una_clave_real

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### OpenAPI
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi.json

### Evento LIVE (inicio de transmisión)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/qforest/streams
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "camera_device_id": "CLA58",
  "datetime": "2026-10-27T15:32:24.935000+00:00",
  "url": "wss://hls.media.qforest.online/qforest/CLA58",
  "electromagnetic_spectrum": "combined",
  "state": "LIVE"
}

### Evento DEFERRED (fin de transmisión)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/qforest/streams
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "camera_device_id": "CLA58",
  "datetime": "2026-10-27T15:40:00.000000+00:00",
  "url": "wss://hls.media.qforest.online/qforest/CLA58",
  "electromagnetic_spectrum": "combined",
  "state": "DEFERRED"
}

### Sin API key (espera 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/qforest/streams
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "camera_device_id": "CLA58",
  "datetime": "2026-10-27T15:32:24.935000+00:00",
  "url": "wss://hls.media.qforest.online/qforest/CLA58",
  "state": "LIVE"
}

### Payload inválido (espera 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/qforest/streams
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "camera_device_id": "CLA58",
  "datetime": "2026-10-27T15:32:24",
  "url": "https://hls.media.qforest.online/qforest/CLA58",
  "state": "LIVE"
}
